This is actually a fantastic setup. Because your NotificationWriterService is already wired up with JPA and uses StringRedisTemplate to broadcast messages, your React frontend will be able to display real-time popup alerts the second a batch advances!
Since you already have the core service built, we just need to add **two new helper methods** to it to handle the Maker's submission and the "Exclude Creator" routing logic. Then, we will inject those perfectly into your VoucherRequestServiceImpl.
Here are the exact code updates you need to make to both files.
### 1. Update NotificationWriterService.java
Add these two helper methods at the bottom of your existing file.
Notice how createNextStepApprovalNotification deliberately passes BOTH the userToExclude and the targetRoleId to the core method. This triggers your database design rule: *"In a scenario where both role and userId are provided, the userId will be excluded."*
```java
    // ==================================================================================
    // NEW HELPER METHODS (Add these to your existing NotificationWriterService)
    // ==================================================================================

    /**
     * Alerts the Maker that their batch was successfully sent to the workflow pipeline.
     */
    public void createBatchSubmissionNotification(String batchId, String creatorId) {
        String message = "Your Batch '" + batchId + "' was submitted successfully.";
        createNotification(creatorId, null, message, "/journal-posting-status", batchId, "JournalService");
    }

    /**
     * Alerts the Checkers that a batch is waiting for them.
     * By passing userToExclude to the userId parameter, your database natively excludes them 
     * from the targetRole blast, preventing self-approval alerts.
     */
    public void createNextStepApprovalNotification(String batchId, String userToExclude, String targetRoleId) {
        String message = "Journal Batch '" + batchId + "' has advanced to your stage and requires your review.";
        createNotification(userToExclude, targetRoleId, message, "/journal-authorization", batchId, "JournalService");
    }

```
